keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T14:25:40-07:00","id":1464641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464639#post1464639\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I suppose they realized that Infernalists would require Blood Sorcery rituals.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, getting a couple more Blood Sorcery rituals would have been nice!<br /> <br /> Btw, the two Blood Sorcery rituals connected to Blood Resonance and Dyscrasias are really good, and probably the best mechanics in the book. <br /> <br /> I reallt like the Circulatory System as villains, and the cult fit neatly as one of their good customers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 10-20-2021, 05:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T19:17:59-07:00","id":1464676,"title":"","content":"Does the Tremere section mention Schreck? Because that &quot;cult&quot; sounds like something he would support, or even create.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-20T22:54:16-07:00","id":1464698,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464676#post1464676\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Tremere section mention Schreck? Because that &amp;quot;cult&amp;quot; sounds like something he would support, or even create.</div> </div> </div> </div>Strangely not, they are Meerlinda fanboys","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T00:05:23-07:00","id":1464705,"title":"","content":"Seems like the hopes for Clan Tremere in V5 which I <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449302-tremere-pyramid-rebuilt?p=1456080#post1456080\">wrote about recently</a> are being realized to at least an extent <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464617#post1464617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">4 is nonsense. Consider me unenthused.</div> </div> </div> </div>During the medieval times the Tremere embraced some persons with martial experience and inclinations to defend the Clan, so I would not consider this that unusual.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers#post1464604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> One of the major cults is the Tremere orthodox cult: The Praesidium.<br /> <br /> They're partying like it's 1992 and looking for Merlinda that they are SURE is still alive.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Were the Praesidium followers of Meerlinda before the recent V5 troubles? Are there some specific reasons or signs that influenced their decision to seek out her in particular?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3254,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","user":"Muad'Dib","date":". 10-21-2021, 07:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T01:38:49-07:00","id":1464707,"title":"","content":"No Baali. Sad face.<br /> Hecata continue their running lead for the best-supported clan in the game, getting yet another exclusive loresheet.<br /> The Tremere loresheet is kinda nice, others I'm not very enthused about. Blood Asceticism seems worse for being a blood ascetic than the corebook Golconda loresheet.<br /> I don't really understand what is the benefit of Gehenna Cults 5. I guess you could pick it as a Tremere and not need a mentor for any blood magic ever? It's a weird benefit (and I don't mean &quot;oveerpowered'), maybe I'm missing something.<br /> <br /> Overall, it's more or less an antagonist book with a bunch of vampire cults (and a Tremere cop squad) for you to fight. Not what I wanted out of a book on forbidden religions, but it's probably helpful to someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T01:42:53-07:00","id":1464708,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464705#post1464705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">S<br /> During the medieval times the Tremere embraced some persons with martial experience and inclinations to defend the Clan, so I would not consider this that unusual.</div> </div> </div> </div>1 But it isn't medieval times. <br /> 2 Does exercise really work with Vampires? Tearing apart muscles to rebuild them doesn't really work when you repair yourself perfectly every dusk. A long distance run doesn't really help anything when there's no oxygen issue for unbreathing vampires. Now you could argue the symbolic gesture of exercise has some magical effect in making the undead more fit, but I think it's equally (and preferably more) likely vampires gain attributes through either feeding from those with the desired traits or, in the case of Tremere, some kind of ritual/self enlightenment process.<br /> 3: <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">For people who used to be able to start fires with their mind, physical exercise seems like a massive case of wasted time and diminishing returns. </span></span></span> Doing jumping jacks as a vampire really just reinforces the idea that this is a cult that wants to break it's members down. And that's my issue; Why is the normal orthodoxy of the one of the most intellectually gifted clans now caricatured as a stupid macho military cult?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T01:51:21-07:00","id":1464709,"title":"","content":"You are making some weird-ass claims. Non-magical combat Tremere are and have always been a thing. Path of Blood used to be extremely conducive to blood buffing and tearing shit up with a gun or sword. Talisman provided a dice bonus when used as a weapon. Blood Cauldron requires a melee touch attack. Yes, mechanically the superior way to fight is learning Movement of Mind and launching everyone into the stratosphere to die of falling damage. But narratively people did not do that.<br /> <br /> As for the last question - Praesidium are not the Tremere Orthodoxy. They are the Black Hand of the Tremere Orthodoxy. Praesidium is a militant strike team enforcing the will of their leaders. They are not paid to think.<br /> <br /> They do get the old Blood Contract ritual as a merit though. Weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","user":"Kammerer","date":". 10-21-2021, 04:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T04:05:04-07:00","id":1464716,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464707#post1464707\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No Baali. Sad face.<br /> Hecata continue their running lead for the best-supported clan in the game, getting yet another exclusive loresheet.<br /> The Tremere loresheet is kinda nice, others I'm not very enthused about. Blood Asceticism seems worse for being a blood ascetic than the corebook Golconda loresheet.<br /> <b>I don't really understand what is the benefit of Gehenna Cults 5. </b>I guess you could pick it as a Tremere and not need a mentor for any blood magic ever? It's a weird benefit (and I don't mean &quot;oveerpowered'), maybe I'm missing something.<br /> <br /> Overall, it's more or less an antagonist book with a bunch of vampire cults (and a Tremere cop squad) for you to fight. Not what I wanted out of a book on forbidden religions, but it's probably helpful to someone.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, it is a supplement to a book about vampire cults. Kind of limited by the fact that it's a Kickstarter Reward.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464708#post1464708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3: <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">For people who used to be able to start fires with their mind, physical exercise seems like a massive case of wasted time and diminishing returns. </span></span></span> Doing jumping jacks as a vampire really just reinforces the idea that this is a cult that wants to break it's members down. And that's my issue; Why is the normal orthodoxy of the one of the most intellectually gifted clans now caricatured as a stupid macho military cult?</div> </div> </div> </div>How do mages raise their physical stats in your game?<br /> <br /> And even then, combat training with magic would involve physical attributes. Mind you, it seems like you're focusing on Rule 4 versus the whole, &quot;Rebuilding the Pyramid&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> I thought you'd be all over that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T04:55:11-07:00","id":1464724,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464705#post1464705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like the hopes for Clan Tremere in V5 which I <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1449302-tremere-pyramid-rebuilt?p=1456080#post1456080\">wrote about recently</a> are being realized to at least an extent <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that is exactly their plan: they think that not all the Councillors have fallen, and want to locate survivors, replace the fallen and cast again the bonding ritual that joined the Pyramid together.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464705#post1464705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Were the Praesidium followers of Meerlinda before the recent V5 troubles? Are there some specific reasons or signs that influenced their decision to seek out her in particular?</div> </div> </div> </div>Their chapter says the cult's leader is one of her descendants, and that &quot;<i>she\u2019s their preferred choice to lead the clan despite their devotion to the historic clan structure</i>&quot;, and they believe to have located three possible places in which she's hiding or being kept as prisoner.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T05:08:28-07:00","id":1464725,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> How do mages raise their physical stats in your game? </div> </div> </div>Mortal mages? Physical exercise or esoteric, idiosyncratic rituals. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> Vampires? Feeding from people with the desired traits or esoteric, idiosyncratic rituals. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464716#post1464716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Mind you, it seems like you're focusing on Rule 4 versus the whole, &quot;Rebuilding the Pyramid&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> I thought you'd be all over that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well I'd rather have &quot;rebuilding the pyramid&quot; be the mainstream Tremere thought rather than something a small bunch of brainwashed nutters are doing. I mean, I'm not opposed to Tremere radically shifting into wargear to get things back in order, but they can do so with the Lure of Flames or scores of well funded, well Dominated henchmen. Tremere aren't warrior salubri, and I kinda feel like the writers are trying to shame Tremere fans by suggesting that the real loyalists to the old pyramid must be tactless lunatics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T05:10:57-07:00","id":1464726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464708#post1464708\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1 But it isn't medieval times.<br /> 2 Does exercise really work with Vampires? Tearing apart muscles to rebuild them doesn't really work when you repair yourself perfectly every dusk. A long distance run doesn't really help anything when there's no oxygen issue for unbreathing vampires. Now you could argue the symbolic gesture of exercise has some magical effect in making the undead more fit, but I think it's equally (and preferably more) likely vampires gain attributes through either feeding from those with the desired traits or, in the case of Tremere, some kind of ritual/self enlightenment process.<br /> 3: <span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">For people who used to be able to start fires with their mind, physical exercise seems like a massive case of wasted time and diminishing returns. </span></span></span> Doing jumping jacks as a vampire really just reinforces the idea that this is a cult that wants to break it's members down. And that's my issue; Why is the normal orthodoxy of the one of the most intellectually gifted clans now caricatured as a stupid macho military cult?</div> </div> </div> </div>They are no macho, they wish to reclaim lost magical artifacts, defeat House Carna and House Ipsisssimus, and &quot;<i>Make Tremere Great Again</i>&quot;, by reinstalling the Pyramid and taking the Tremere back to their days of free magical experimentation.<br /> <br /> Their military bent doesn't seem that out ot place: in the old Ars Magica book, the Tremere example character was a swordsman, after all, and Tremere were the undisputed master of wizard duelling. So, harking back at those mythical times seems appropriate for a militant group.<br /> <br /> To me, they don't seem nutters at all, just a radical group engaged in covert war with other Tremere factions. Hardly strange, in a fractured society with strong tensions between competing factions: leaders may sit at discussiont tables, but on the ground some clashes are bound to happen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12590,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","user":"Manfr","date":". 10-21-2021, 08:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T05:40:20-07:00","id":1464727,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464716#post1464716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Well, it is a supplement to a book about vampire cults. Kind of limited by the fact that it's a Kickstarter Reward.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> 1)How do mages raise their physical stats in your game?<br /> <br /> 2)And even then, combat training with magic would involve physical attributes. Mind you, it seems like you're focusing on Rule 4 versus the whole, &quot;Rebuilding the Pyramid&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> I thought you'd be all over that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> 1) Mortals? Working out, running etc. Vampires? Esoterica and age. <br /> <br /> 2) Lure of the Flames, Path of the Levinbolt and Movement of the mind beg to differ, (tho Path of Mars agrees)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T06:37:40-07:00","id":1464730,"title":"","content":"Relevant: Path of Mars is a garbage waste of XP, and is really only popular among Sabbat.<br /> Tremere are all about using their minds to destroy foes. Brute physical training has never been their modus operandi. They've got Ghouls and Gargoyles for that.<br /> <br /> Lure of flames doesn't exist anymore. (much to V5's detriment) <br /> <br /> The Odd Tremere knight came in during the Dark ages but that's because the Tremere were in a bind and needed effective troops fast; LoF isn't combat viable till the third level, but one thaumaturge with burning blade or the invisibility ritual can make great use of newly embraced vampire knights, and should these knights survive they can eventually learn magic like Tremere are meant to. Modern weaponry greatly reduces the skill gap between &quot;a week of training&quot; and &quot;training their entire lives&quot;. Tremere don't need to reach peak fitness for a little advantage over their enemies when they can pick up something that's point and kill, and Tremere are going to have a lot of difficulty trying to win swordfights against other vampires as one of the only three clans that doesn't have a single physical discipline. <br /> <br /> Maybe in context with V5's simplistic combat rules and absence of magic, it makes sense to have physically focused Tremere. But for OG VTM, it doesn't at all make a lick of sense beyond &quot;macho bullshit appeals to fascists and these Tremere are clearly fascist&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25794,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","user":"MyWifeIsScary","date":". 10-21-2021, 09:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary"