 target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 10-21-2021, 10:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T06:47:23-07:00","id":1464732,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464730#post1464730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Relevant: Path of Mars is a garbage waste of XP, and is really only popular among Sabbat.<br /> Tremere are all about using their minds to destroy foes. Brute physical training has never been their modus operandi. They've got Gargoyles for that.<br /> <br /> Lure of flames doesn't exist anymore. (much to V5's detriment)</div> </div> </div> </div>Physical Tremere so much have never been a thing that Tremere books featured multiple physical Tremere characters. Just to show how much not a thing it is.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/fZdVNos.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/ukW7PW0.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"https://i.imgur.com/BjkbkAd.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/></div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T06:58:20-07:00","id":1464733,"title":"","content":"1- An exception and explicitly an embrace of circumstances.<br /> 2- That's a social character who uses his physique as an advantage, not a combat character.<br /> 3 An unsanctioned embrace. Almost a Caitiff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T07:34:24-07:00","id":1464737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464730#post1464730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> &quot;macho bullshit appeals to fascists and these Tremere are clearly fascist&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>I really love the Tremere, but well ... if there is a vampiric organization that is fascist in its outlook, it's clearly the Tremere Pyramid. It is hierarchic but apparently meritocratic, based on a mobilising ideology and on the cult of personality of the Leader, it controls or tries to control every aspect of the lives of its members, it has lots of paraphernalia to create distinctions and rewards the faithful, and preaches constant war mobilization against external threats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T08:29:00-07:00","id":1464739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464737#post1464737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I really love the Tremere, but well ... if there is a vampiric organization that is fascist in its outlook, it's clearly the Tremere Pyramid. It is hierarchic but apparently meritocratic, based on a mobilising ideology and on the cult of personality of the Leader, it controls or tries to control every aspect of the lives of its members, it has lots of paraphernalia to create distinctions and rewards the faithful, and preaches constant war mobilization against external threats.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean that's a weird statement to make given it lacks the death worship of fascism, nationalism, militaristic, and mobilization against the outsider. It seems significantly less fascist than the Sabbat.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T08:39:07-07:00","id":1464741,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464739#post1464739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean that's a weird statement to make given it lacks the death worship of fascism, nationalism, militaristic, and mobilization against the outsider. It seems significantly less fascist than the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>The sabbat isn't fascist, despite the clumsy writing of v5. Loosely speaking pre 5th it was a theocratic constitutional monarchy post 5 it's just decentralised warlords ala da europe at its worst.....if I'm being charitable since the writing contradicts itself in several places","signature":"","edited":{"userid":26986,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","user":"Ragged Robin","date":". 10-21-2021, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T08:57:07-07:00","id":1464744,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464739#post1464739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean that's a weird statement to make given it lacks the death worship of fascism, nationalism, militaristic, and mobilization against the outsider. It seems significantly less fascist than the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I call it more like a feudal guild tbh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T08:57:50-07:00","id":1464745,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464724#post1464724\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Their chapter says the cult's leader is one of her descendants, and that &quot;<i>she\u2019s their preferred choice to lead the clan despite their devotion to the historic clan structure</i>&quot;, and they believe to have located three possible places in which she's hiding or being kept as prisoner.</div> </div> </div> </div>How nice for a member of a Bloodline to be loyal all the way no matter the circumstances.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T09:05:07-07:00","id":1464748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464741#post1464741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The sabbat isn't fascist, despite the clumsy writing of v5. Loosely speaking pre 5th it was a theocratic constitutional monarchy post 5 it's just decentralised warlords ala da europe at its worst.....if I'm being charitable since the writing contradicts itself in several places</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm a huge Sabbat fan but calling it a constitutional monarchy is like describing the Manson family as a hippie commune. I mean, technically true, but in the loosest sense.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T09:08:57-07:00","id":1464749,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464739#post1464739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I mean that's a weird statement to make given it lacks the death worship of fascism, nationalism, militaristic, and mobilization against the outsider. It seems significantly less fascist than the Sabbat.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tremere are absolutely nationalistic, in the sense of their Clan culture, and constantly mobilizing against outsiders: their whole propaganda is based on siege mentality and sacrifice for the Pyramid. <br /> <br /> The Sabbat is even more evidently fascist, it has all the added thuggery and bravado of early blackshirts, and the suprematist and genocidal tendencies of the Nazis.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T09:12:11-07:00","id":1464751,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ragged Robin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464741#post1464741\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The sabbat isn't fascist, despite the clumsy writing of v5. Loosely speaking pre 5th it was a theocratic constitutional monarchy post 5 it's just decentralised warlords ala da europe at its worst.....if I'm being charitable since the writing contradicts itself in several places</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually, many studies on the institutional structure of Nazism underline that, under the allmighty Leader, there was huge bureaucratic chaos and decentralization, with Ministers, Gauleiters and Party leaders jockeying for power. So, the two aspects can paradoxically stand together. <br /> <br /> Of course, no faction by itself is a perfect metaphor of some mortal ideology, and this is good for realism: ideologies arise from concrete circustamces, and the life of a Vampire is markedly different from the life of a Mortal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T09:28:47-07:00","id":1464753,"title":"","content":"Authoritarian =/= Fascist. <br /> <br /> The Tremere have always supported the Camarilla. They've supported other clans in the Camarilla; It's in their best interests to. They rarely try to become princes, because authority for the sake of authority doesn't really appeal to them. They have a lot of conceit around thaumaturgy and go to great lengths to uphold their monopoly, but that's just capitalism, not a fascist streak. Hermeticism isn't a fascist faith. It's actually one of the most inclusive. <br /> <br /> Sure, they'll get funny when you talk to them about Salubri. But how often does that happen? The Salubri are dead! <br /> <br /> The Tremere are a corporation. A company. A business. Sure they don't let their members leave, but they do invest a lot more into their members than any real business will. A management structure isn't fascism. Company loyalty isn't fascism. Competitiveness isn't fascism. Tremere don't care about ideas, they care about profit. And destroying, sabotaging and discouraging the competition keeps the profit secure. If the Tremere thought they had more to gain than to lose by reviving the salubri and holding hands with the Tzmisce, they'd do it. A fascist wouldn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T09:42:33-07:00","id":1464754,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464748#post1464748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a huge Sabbat fan but calling it a constitutional monarchy is like describing the Manson family as a hippie commune. I mean, technically true, but in the loosest sense.</div> </div> </div> </div>Morality is irrelevant when describing government types. We're talking about how it's organized and not how humaine it is.<br /> Plus plenty of historical constitutional monarchies have been positively vile.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T09:43:25-07:00","id":1464755,"title":"","content":"In terms of the martial Tremere;<br /> A - The game should be user friendly enough to allow for players who want to run martial minded Tremere.<br /> B- There had always been a place for such characters, as others have demonstrated.<br /> C- Lore of the Clans included at least two character concepts for such types.<br /> <br /> So none of this is new and none of it goes against the rules as written or even as simply implied.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T09:44:51-07:00","id":1464756,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464618#post1464618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You need Tremere who can fight.<br /> <br /> So of course they practice combat magic and dodge rolls.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fun fact: in the DA line it was clearly stated (Libellus Sanguinis IIRC) that right at their beginning as a clan the Tremere embraced wizards AND grogs. The former for their knowledge in order to grow the mystichal might of the clan, the latter because they needed able soldiers capable to go toe to toe with the Szlachta and to act as bodyguards for the magi of the clan. So having Tremere who can fight, especially after the fall of the pyramid makes ample sense.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T09:46:20-07:00","id":1464757,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Manfr</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464751#post1464751\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Actually, many studies on the institutional structure of Nazism underline that, under the allmighty Leader, there was huge bureaucratic chaos and decentralization, with Ministers, Gauleiters and Party leaders jockeying for power. So, the two aspects can paradoxically stand together. <br /> <br /> Of course, no faction by itself is a perfect metaphor of some mortal ideology, and this is good for realism: ideologies arise from concrete circustamces, and the life of a Vampire is markedly different from the life of a Mortal.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting but the Sabbat doesn't really have any traits uniquely linked with fascism and very few of the traits genrally linked with it. Its supremacist and militant which is so vague most world governments qualify as some stage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26986-ragged-robin","name":"Ragged Robin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26986_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T09:46:51-07:00","id":1464758,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464731#post1464731\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yes it does. It's in Cults of the Blood Gods under the Church of Caine.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it doesn't.... unless you mean this crappy ritual;<br /> <br /> <i><u><b>Creatio Ignis</b></u><br /> The caster of this Ritual diverts hungry flame from their flesh, using an enchanted coating of vitae like a buffer and can set items and people alight using the fire.<br /> <br /> This Ritual is a phenomenal breach of the Masquerade as the power is entirely visible and can cause intense environmental feedback, not to mention the bloody coating of the caster\u2019s hands before activation.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Ingredients:</b> Sufficient vitae (from any vampire) to coat the caster\u2019s arms up to the elbows, a source of flame (such as a lighter).<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 Process:</b> The vampire immerses their arms in the blood and withstands the urge to feed or frenzy. After extracting their arms, exposure to flame will ignite the vitae rather than the vampire it coats. The vampire can then go on to set targets alight using the fire on their skin.<br /> <br /> <b>\u2022 System:</b> If the user is at Hunger 4 or more, make a hunger frenzy test at Difficulty 3 to avoid draining the ingredients. At any point during the night they may expose the vitae to fire and make a Ritual roll. A win ignites flames on the vampire\u2019s hands and arms, which in a spectacular display provoke a terror frenzy test (Difficulty 2) in all nearby vampires except the caster. They may touch others with Dexterity + Brawl in physical combat to inflict two Aggravated Health damage. Entering a grapple ignites the other person\u2019s clothes, continuing the damage each turn until a Composure + Survival roll (Difficulty 3) is won to end the burn. The caster is only resistant to flame on their arms, and will burn as usual elsewhere. The fiery arms extinguish when the caster wills it or when the scene ends.</i><br /> <br /> That's A) a level 5 ritual, B) melee only, and C) you have to coat your arms in blood and leave it there until you ignite it with fire from an outside source. To do it again requires re-coating your arms and lighting it again.<br /> <br /> Here's the ACTUAL The Lure of Flames;<br /> <br /> <i><b>The Lure of Flames</b><br /> This path grants the thaumaturge the ability to conjure forth mystical flames \u2014 small fires at first, but skilled magicians may create great conflagrations. Fire created by this path is not \u201cnatural.\u201d In fact, many vampires believe the flames to be conjured from Hell itself. The Lure of Flames is greatly feared, as fire is one of the surest ways to bring Final Death upon a vampire. See \u201cFire\u201d (p. 297) for more information on how vampires suffer from flame.<br /> <br /> Fire conjured by The Lure of Flames must be released for it to have any effect. Thus, a \u201cpalm of flame\u201d does not burn the vampire\u2019s hand and cause an aggravated wound (nor does it cause the caster to frenzy) \u2014 it merely produces light. Once the flame has been released, however, it burns normally and the character has no control over it.<br /> <br /> <b>System:</b> The number of successes determines how accurately the vampire places the flame in his desired location (declared before the roll is made). One success is all that is necessary to conjure a flame in one\u2019s hand, while five successes place a flame anywhere in the Kindred\u2019s line of sight. Less successes mean that the flame appears somewhere at the Storyteller\u2019s discretion<br /> \u2014 as a rough rule of thumb, the thaumaturge can accurately place a flame within 10 yards or meters of themselves per success.<br /> <br /> Individual descriptions are not provided for each level of this path \u2014 fire is fire, after all (including potentially causing frenzy in other vampires witnessing it). The chart below describes the path level required to generate a specific amount of flame. To soak the damage at all, a vampire must have the Fortitude Discipline. Fire under the caster\u2019s control does not harm<br /> the vampire or cause him to frenzy, but fires started as a result of the unnatural flame affect the thaumaturge normally.<br /> <br /> \u2022 Candle (difficulty 3 to soak, one health level of aggravated damage/turn)<br /> \u2022\u2022 Palm of flame (difficulty 4 to soak, one health level of aggravated damage/turn)<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022 Campfire (difficulty 5 to soak, two health levels of aggravated damage/turn)<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Bonfire (difficulty 7 to soak, two health levels of aggravated damage/turn)<br /> \u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022 Inferno (difficulty 9 to soak, three health levels of aggravated damage/turn)</i><br /> <br /> Trying to claim that V5 ritual is the same thing as The Lure of Flames is like trying to claim a guy flying a toy remote control helicopter from his canoe is the same thing as an aircraft carrier.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T10:15:27-07:00","id":1464766,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464753#post1464753\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Authoritarian =/= Fascist.<br /> <br /> The Tremere have always supported the Camarilla. They've supported other clans in the Camarilla; It's in their best interests to. They rarely try to become princes, because authority for the sake of authority doesn't really appeal to them. They have a lot of conceit around thaumaturgy and go to great lengths to uphold their monopoly, but that's just capitalism, not a fascist streak. Hermeticism isn't a fascist faith. It's actually one of the most inclusive.<br /> <br /> Sure, they'll get funny when you talk to them about Salubri. But how often does that happen? The Salubri are dead!<br /> <br /> The Tremere are a corporation. A company. A business. Sure they don't let their members leave, but they do invest a lot more into their members than any real business will. A management structure isn't fascism. Company loyalty isn't fascism. Competitiveness isn't fascism. Tremere don't care about ideas, they care about profit. And destroying, sabotaging and discouraging the competition keeps the profit secure. If the Tremere thought they had more to gain than to lose by reviving the salubri and holding hands with the Tzmisce, they'd do it. A fascist wouldn't.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> I'm well aware of the difference between Fascism and Autoritharianism, I've studied Juan Linz: on the scale between the two poles, Ventrue make far more better Autoritharians (Horty, Monarchical Yugoslavia, South American regimes) than Tremere. Tremere of course lack any populist tone, but then there were a lot of fascist intellectuals and of fascist technocrats: Heidegger was no populist and Francoist Spain after WW2 was a clerical / technocratic hybrid. <br /> <br /> Tremere work wonderfully also as Eastern Bloc Communists or as a Pinochet-style military-technocratic junta.<br /> <br /> In any case, I wouldn't gent stuck on &quot;this Clan is X&quot;: the beauty of the game is that each Clan and Sect can be used for so many different metaphors and situations.<br /> <br /> Tremere can easily fill the roles of:<br /> <br /> -Autoritharian tecnocratic regime<br /> -Fascist regime<br /> -Tech startup<br /> -Yuppies<br /> -Academic department<br /> -Masonic lodge<br /> -Research group<br /> <br /> and a wide variety of other roles. The same is true for the other factions of the game (at least, the well designed one).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T10:23:55-07:00","id":1464769,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464748#post1464748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'm a huge Sabbat fan but calling it a constitutional monarchy is like describing the Manson family as a hippie commune. I mean, technically true, but in the loosest sense.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> it scans pretty well onto a monarchy, a really nasty quasi theocratic one, but that has been several real world monarchies, it also scans onto flat out theocracy as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T10:29:42-07:00","id":1464772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464755#post1464755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In terms of the martial Tremere;<br /> A - The game should be user friendly enough to allow for players who want to run martial minded Tremere.<br /> B- There had always been a place for such characters, as others have demonstrated.<br /> C- Lore of the Clans included at least two character concepts for such types.<br /> <br /> So none of this is new and none of it goes against the rules as written or even as simply implied.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're conflating things. <br /> <br /> Martially minded Tremere in modern times are fine. As individuals. <br /> <br /> Making an ultra-orthodox ultra-martial cult out of them? That says a lot about the rest of the clan, and I don't like it. Making the most pro-house Tremere group a right wing <i>cult </i>of extremists goes a long way in justifying and giving the moral highground to House Carna and Ippisimus while de-legitimizing standard-issue Tremere who want to fight rebels in a more practical manner. <br /> <br /> One should also consider how this effects the &quot;Vienna prime was an inside job&quot; theories. <br /> This also directly contradicts what was stated in V5: that the different Tremere houses feel they shouldn't destroy eachother because their blood tells them not to. (or maybe that's just the leaders) <br /> <br /> <br /> Maybe I'd rather just <i>not blow up Vienna </i>or perhaps <i>have the Tremere orthodoxy make the most rational decision and immediately purge the traitors so none of this shit would happen. </i> I mean &quot;<i>we totally wanted this to happen but also here's a cult that doesn't&quot; </i>is justifiable, but it isn't good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T10:38:20-07:00","id":1464774,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taggie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464769#post1464769\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">it scans pretty well onto a monarchy, a really nasty quasi theocratic one, but that has been several real world monarchies, it also scans onto flat out theocracy as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>If there's no hereditary elements to a monarchy, isn't it just a dictatorship?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T10:43:23-07:00","id":1464775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464774#post1464774\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If there's no hereditary elements to a monarchy, isn't it just a dictatorship?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Nope, there have been Elective Monarchies before, Holy Roman Empire, Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth, Mongol Empire, Unified Silla and on and on, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elective_monarchy\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elective_monarchy</a> Arguably the Papal States as well. They are different things, I mean it might be hair splitting, but I would bet the IC inspiration for the Sabbat Regent system was the Papal States, whether that was the goal from the start, or retconned on later is an open question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T11:19:49-07:00","id":1464781,"title":"","content":"As I recall, most elective monarchies devolve into hereditary monarchies.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/490-omenseer","name":"omenseer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar490_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"987"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T11:25:11-07:00","id":1464782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>omenseer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464781#post1464781\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As I recall, most elective monarchies devolve into hereditary monarchies.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Pretty much. It's a flaw in the system, which is why it's pretty much extinct, apart from the Papacy and a few technical forms.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25011-taggie","name":"Taggie","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1047"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-21T15:24:59-07:00","id":1464800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464627#post1464627\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This book is mostly material cut from CotBG?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, we don't make books using cut material. This is all newly written for this book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","e