tline of a loresheet for the 1444 Chamber, covering the privileges of serving them I suppose. I also saw loresheets for the Rosselini and Milliner families, but maybe those are from another supplement or even the final edition of <i>Cults of the Blood Gods</i>.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3523-spencer-from-the-hills","name":"Spencer from The Hills","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"546"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T15:58:02-07:00","id":1464930,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464907#post1464907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Gehenna cults.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about &quot;RUINOUS BELIEFS&quot;?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T16:08:47-07:00","id":1464931,"title":"","content":"So, if it\u2019s covering Gehenna cults, does it talk at all about how the belief in Cyclical Gehennas becoming more accepted affects their beliefs?<br /> <br /> Ex. how does The Last Daughter of Eve work if there are multiple Gehennas? Is it the same person each time? Reincarnation? \u201cLast\u201d isn\u2019t actually THE last just the most current last?<br /> <br /> Seeing some of these cults squirm trying to square their doctrines with new evidence would be something I\u2019d find amusing to read about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-22T16:20:08-07:00","id":1464933,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chris24601</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464931#post1464931\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, if it\u2019s covering Gehenna cults, does it talk at all about how the belief in Cyclical Gehennas becoming more accepted affects their beliefs?<br /> <br /> Ex. how does The Last Daughter of Eve work if there are multiple Gehennas? Is it the same person each time? Reincarnation? \u201cLast\u201d isn\u2019t actually THE last just the most current last?<br /> <br /> Seeing some of these cults squirm trying to square their doctrines with new evidence would be something I\u2019d find amusing to read about.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, it doesn't discuss Gehenna cults in general but these specific Gehenna cults.<br /> <br /> * The Whisperers of the Dead are Capuchin worshipers.<br /> * The Orphans of Enoch believe this very much is the FINAL Gehenna even as they rebuild the True Hand. I mean, they never mentionally SPECIFICALLY they're the Tal'Mah'Re's remnants but it's blindingly obvious to anyone familiar with the lore.<br /> * The Third Day are a bunch of Beckoning-ridden Elders struggling to stave it off.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Grumpy RPG Reviews</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464930#post1464930\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What about &quot;RUINOUS BELIEFS&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>Diablerie and infernalist cults, basically.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T18:13:58-07:00","id":1465074,"title":"","content":"will this be available from drivethrurpg, at some point, or is it strictly a kickstarter reward?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>they/them.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27123-littlewitchmaus","name":"littlewitchmaus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27123_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"49"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T18:23:32-07:00","id":1465075,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>littlewitchmaus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1465074#post1465074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">will this be available from drivethrurpg, at some point, or is it strictly a kickstarter reward?</div> </div> </div> </div>As with the other Cults of the Blood Gods related books you'll be able to purchase this via drivethrurpg, I think. I myself downloded it from their site as a reward for supporting the kickstarter.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24992-haquim","name":"Haquim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24992_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-23T20:47:03-07:00","id":1465090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>littlewitchmaus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1465074#post1465074\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">will this be available from drivethrurpg, at some point, or is it strictly a kickstarter reward?</div> </div> </div> </div>It will be made available to the public in time. None of the stretch goals have ever been KS exclusives. Backers just get them early and free.<br /> <br /> I'd imagine it will become available for purchase in a couple of weeks.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://youtu.be/_yBS2EZFduI?t=2m13s\" target=\"_blank\">Homo sapiens. What an inventive, invincible species. It's only a few million years since they crawled up out of the mud and learned to walk. Puny, defenceless bipeds. They've survived flood, famine and plague. They've survived cosmic wars and holocausts. And now, here they are, out among the stars, waiting to begin a new life. Ready to outsit eternity. They're indomitable. Indomitable.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/420-akatsukileader13","name":"AkatsukiLeader13","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar420_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1637"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T03:03:05-07:00","id":1465113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1464933#post1464933\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Diablerie and infernalist cults, basically.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Infernalists&quot; is doing a lot of work here. The four &quot;Ruinous Beliefs&quot; cults are:<ul><li>A blood abstaining cult where the founder has a magical way to diablerize his followers without getting the diablerie marks (but apparently hasn't done a whole lot of diablerie yet since he still has Humanity 3)</li> <li>Canadian neo-vikings worshipping a torpid Gangrel methuselah</li> <li>&quot;Rich White Male&quot; British coterie that eats people (how are they a cult or 'ruinous'?)</li> <li>An anarchist personality cult with nega-catholic trappings.</li> </ul><br /> None of them are &quot;infernalists&quot; in the sense of interacting with or worshipping demons.<br /> <br /> Also, I officially nominate <b><i>Seal the Beast's Maw</i></b> for the worst discipline in the game. Like wow man. You are better off not having it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12892,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","user":"Kammerer","date":". 10-24-2021, 06:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-10-24T08:06:21-07:00","id":1465139,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1465113#post1465113\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Infernalists&quot; is doing a lot of work here. The four &quot;Ruinous Beliefs&quot; cults are:<ul><li>A blood abstaining cult where the founder has a magical way to diablerize his followers without getting the diablerie marks (but apparently hasn't done a whole lot of diablerie yet since he still has Humanity 3)</li> <li>Canadian neo-vikings worshipping a torpid Gangrel methuselah</li> <li>&quot;Rich White Male&quot; British coterie that eats people (how are they a cult or 'ruinous'?)</li> <li>An anarchist personality cult with nega-catholic trappings.</li> </ul><br /> <br /> None of them are &quot;infernalists&quot; in the sense of interacting with or worshipping demons.<br /> <br /> Also, I officially nominate <b><i>Seal the Beast's Maw</i></b> for the worst discipline in the game. Like wow man. You are better off not having it.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Soldiers of the Adversary is an Infernalist cult. Wannabes or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-11-02T08:56:37-07:00","id":1466291,"title":"","content":"Question to all the wiseguys here. I'm reading Forbidden Religions, and struggling to understand what the four-dot merit &quot;Cult Breaker&quot; in Forbidden Religions is supposed to do.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Once per story for a scene, while socially interacting with you, cult members do not benefit from any dots in Status they may have within their own cult. </div> </div> </div>I mean... huh? Status <i>is</i> an in-group thing. If I'm not a cult member, then Status (Cult) doesn't affect me anyway. I don't need any special merit for that. And if the intended use is &quot;you are infiltrating a cult and get into a rap battle with another cultist while doing so&quot;, then that seems to be insanely niche for a 4-dot once-per-story merit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-14T02:32:46-08:00","id":1472416,"title":"","content":"I entered this forum and topic looking for info about this book, and I have found a theme that is 80% about<b></b>: Tremere, fascists, V5 poopoo, etc. I would like to see and read more in depth debates, about the book, instead the infinite loop of 5th edition haters and fans arguing.<br /> <br /> I would like, for example, more information about this return of the &quot;presummed Talmahera&quot; or the disciples of Ur-Shulgi.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> Kammerer, I think that this merit could make reference to techniques to avoid brainwashing and indoctrination, cancelling the effects on other characters of being members of the cult.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-14T08:48:21-08:00","id":1472446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1472416#post1472416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I entered this forum and topic looking for info about this book, and I have found a theme that is 80% about<b></b>: Tremere, fascists, V5 poopoo, etc. I would like to see and read more in depth debates, about the book, instead the infinite loop of 5th edition haters and fans arguing.<br /> <br /> I would like, for example, more information about this return of the &quot;presummed Talmahera&quot; or the disciples of Ur-Shulgi.</div> </div> </div> </div><b>1. Presumed Tal Mahe Ra</b> (<b>Orphans of Enoch</b>): Presumably the remnants of the True Black Hand, it doesn't speak much about the destruction of Enoch, just that the remnants are traumatized by it, but little attention is given to it overall. The Cult itself seeks to hasten Gehenna, by making sure its portents come to fruition.<br /> <br /> <b>2. Disciples of Ur-Shulgi: </b>Fanatical to Haqim, seek to destroy the unfaithful to him. Notably, they are interest in Thin-Bloods and their Alchemy.<br /> <br /> On the Cult status thing, it is completely reasonable that one would benefit from high status in a cult even when interacting with another who seeks to break their faith. You wouldn't easily be able to make the Metropolitan of the Church of Caine question their Faith, while an initiate might be easier.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":27145,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","user":"SetiteFriend","date":". 01-14-2022, 11:51 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27145-setitefriend","name":"SetiteFriend","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27145_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"255"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-15T11:09:27-08:00","id":1472509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1472416#post1472416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would like to see and read more in depth debates, about the book, instead the infinite loop of 5th edition haters and fans arguing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good luck with that - that is what all the discussions turn into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-17T19:18:22-08:00","id":1472636,"title":"","content":"I\u2019m a long time Tremere fan and I actually like the Praesidium. I think it it makes sense that they would have an interest in combat, in fact I have often thought that the idea of martially focused Tremere was cool and made sense. The Tremere aren\u2019t just scholars, they are a secret society that wants power, they should occasionally make use of violence against their enemies. In fact, considering the origins of the Tremere as masters of magical duels, their wars with the Tzimisce and the Order of Hermes, it seems natural that they should have a tradition of martial expertise.<br /> <br /> I would like to see some rules that facilitate that idea, like new Thau, um, I mean Blood Sorcery powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1129-sergeant-brother","name":"Sergeant Brother","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1129_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1620"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-18T10:50:56-08:00","id":1472679,"title":"","content":"When will this book be available to general buyers, or on the Vault?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T19:15:48-08:00","id":1473373,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/374548/Forbidden-Religions-Vampire-the-Masquerade-5th-Edition?src=newest&amp;filters=45623_45624_45645\" target=\"_blank\">The book has appeared on the Vault. </a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-26T22:27:44-08:00","id":1473382,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>SetiteFriend</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1472446#post1472446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <b>1. Presumed Tal Mahe Ra</b> (<b>Orphans of Enoch</b>): Presumably the remnants of the True Black Hand, it doesn't speak much about the destruction of Enoch, just that the remnants are traumatized by it, but little attention is given to it overall. The Cult itself seeks to hasten Gehenna, by making sure its portents come to fruition.<br /> <br /> <b>2. Disciples of Ur-Shulgi: </b>Fanatical to Haqim, seek to destroy the unfaithful to him. Notably, they are interest in Thin-Bloods and their Alchemy.<br /> <br /> On the Cult status thing, it is completely reasonable that one would benefit from high status in a cult even when interacting with another who seeks to break their faith. You wouldn't easily be able to make the Metropolitan of the Church of Caine question their Faith, while an initiate might be easier.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I'm actually going to respond to this and other elements because <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar24202_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"24202\" data-vbnamecard=\"24202\">Justycar</a> is right that we might ACTUALLY talk about the book in this thread about the book. Crazy, I know.<br /> <br /> My opinion on the above two is as good a place to start as any and I'm going to speak to my thoughts regarding them in bullet points.<br /> <br /> 1. <b>OPP's help</b>: I think Onyx Path has pretty much been carrying water for 5th Edition from the beginning and a large part of that has been patching holes and spackling the holes in the setting, One thing Onyx Path has an interest in that Paradox Interactive doesn't is revisiting old material. 5th Edition was supposed to be something of a clean slate and jumping on point. Which makes sense because only the die hards (like the people here) wanted to follow up on plots that haven't been followed up on for 15 years. BJD aside.<br /> <br /> Well they DID write BJD so they've been inserting as much material from that book and their own takes on past subject into their bonus books as possible. I'll be honest, without Chicago by Night, Let the Streets Run Red, The Chicago Folios, and Cults of the Blood Gods--I think V5 would have been an artistic failure. I am a stalwart defender of V5 as everyone here knows but let's be honest, I'm a stalwart V5 guy because of what OPP has done with it.<br /> <br /> 2. <b>Disciples of Ur-Shulgi</b>: I think this is a fairly direct adaptation of what they were doing in 3rd Edition and not much of an update. The followers of Ur-Shulgi are killing in the name of Haqim and are the same crazy ass religious terrorists they've always been. I actually was hoping they'd been wiped out by the Sabbat during the Gehenna Crusade since, bluntly, the Sabbat are kind of their antithesis yet similar enough they'd make a b-line straight for one another. Here, Ur-Shulgi just kind of disappears while the take on Alamut in THE BLACK HAND is a great deal different. I see the contradiction here as something bound to have happened eventually but disappointing.<br /> <br /> I can't say too much praise here as while the Disciples of Ur-Shulgi are USEFUL, they're kind of useful in the way the Iron Sheik was in professional wrestling. They're one-dimensional professional heels that exist to be any group of vampires can hate. They do seem a lot less powerful and dangerous than they were in 3rd Edition but it's been 15 years and it seems the Banu Haqim in the Camarilla are still around so they can't have been doing too great.<br /> <br /> 3. <b>Orphans of Enoch</b>: I think the Tal'Ma'Re is kind of a sad scoop up of the concepts introduced in V20's version of the True Hand. They had some fascinating ideas about how to redeem the silly concept of Dirty Secrets and I think we can all agree OPP's version is superior in every way. Unfortunately, Paradox's official opinion seems to be EVERYTHING IS CANON (from the original game) so the nuking of both the Ravnos as well as the Black Hand is 100% correct. So if the Baali did join the True Hand, they were presumably nuked with the rest of Enoch. Such a shame.<br /> <br /> Well these are an okay follow up to the Black Hand but they're not the Black Hand as we know them. They're a bunch of shell-shocked refugees who have lost everything. The fact they were nuked and Gehenna has resulted in nothing but massive death for most Elders (I presume most non-Chatterlings of the True Hand's survivors have been Beckoned), it's understandable why these guys are nothing but a shadow of their former selves.<br /> <br /> In a way too much change vs the Disciples of Ur-Shulgi's lack of change.<br /> <br /> 4. <b>The Praesidium</b>: The Tremere Pyramid getting nuked was one of the changes that pissed off old school V:TM fans the most because the Illuminati within the Illuminati was one of the most popular clans. Remaking the Tremere Pyramid as a smaller, leaner, Kentucky-based version is something I think is a good idea. However, I know plenty of fans who still won't like them because they're a lot more combat focused than the original recipe Tremere rather than a straight recreation.<br /> <br /> However, this makes perfect sense to me because the Tremere have just experienced a catastrophic fucking loss at the hands of the Second Inquisition's hunters. If you don't want to just ignore V5 like some old school fans (you know who you are), then the Tremere survivors deciding they need to take some levels in magic kung fu seems like a reasonable course of action. Too many Tremere have died and too many of their enemies are ready and willing to take the fight to them so investing some Discipline points in combat skills is a pretty good idea--especially since Lure of Flames is no longer available.<br /> <br /> (Jason Carl canonized the lightning bolt, though, so I assume every one of these guys knows that one)<br /> <br /> The biggest failure of this is that they ABSOLUTELY should have included more combat rituals with this group. If they had, it would easily have been the most popular cult here.<br /> <br /> 5. Random aside about the Praesidium but there's no way in hell that it would be located in Lousiville instead of Lexington. Lexington is the land of rich weirdos (including one transplanted Medieval castle), isolated estates, rich creepy inbred families, and the University of Kentucky.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":12002,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","user":"CTPhipps","date":". 01-27-2022, 01:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T14:08:02-08:00","id":1473498,"title":"","content":"As someone form Kentucky, I can tell you exactly why Louisville would be a better fit. The population of Lexington/Fayette Co. is about 250K; Louisville/Jefferson Co. is 650K with a GMA of 1.2 million. The higher population alone could support more vampires. Further, there is a higher amount of business and money there too. For comparison, the international HQ of Yum brands (KFC/Taco Bell/Pizza Hut) is located there. Lexington has the HQ of Long John Silver's (which was founded there)/A &amp; W All-American diners. As to the other factors--the castle is one county over, outside of Lexington proper; the 'isolated' estates are mostly farms (horses/cattle/sheep/llamas, although this last one is iffy), mostly twenty to thirty minutes from downtown depending on the traffic; the 'inbred' family stereotype is more of an eastern Kentucky thing, if your are brave try googling 'Hillbilly Days Pikeville' for an example, just remember that it is for charity; and finally, Lexington is also the home of Transylvania University, the first institute of higher learning west of the Appalachians, a highly ranked private school.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T15:07:01-08:00","id":1473503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1473382#post1473382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> 1. <b>OPP's help</b>: I think Onyx Path has pretty much been carrying water for 5th Edition from the beginning and a large part of that has been patching holes and spackling the holes in the setting, One thing Onyx Path has an interest in that Paradox Interactive doesn't is revisiting old material. 5th Edition was supposed to be something of a clean slate and jumping on point. Which makes sense because only the die hards (like the people here) wanted to follow up on plots that haven't been followed up on for 15 years. BJD aside.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have a bit more nuanced vision of this: the original V5 Team (Ericsson et al.) were very keen for revisiting old material. Far from being a clean slate, V5 Core, Anarchs and Camarilla are loaded with kudos and nods to older material, and seem very much into establishing a direct continuation of the old setting (of course, with some variations).<br /> <br /> Nonetheless, I think we are now in a &quot;soft reboot&quot; moment: with Justin Achilli as Lead Designer, the move towards the &quot;clean slate&quot; is fairly evident, and also openly proclaimed. To be fair, the &quot;clean slate&quot; is also a bit evident in lates OPP stretch books: this is, perhaps, a consequence of Paradox directly taking the lead of the project. After all, Justin has already presided over two fairly huge shake-ups of the setting, Revised (which soft-rebooted many things of Second Edition) and Requiem (which hard-rebooted the whole game).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CTPhipps</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1473382#post1473382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3. <b>Orphans of Enoch</b>: I think the Tal'Ma'Re is kind of a sad scoop up of the concepts introduced in V20's version of the True Hand. They had some fascinating ideas about how to redeem the silly concept of Dirty Secrets and I think we can all agree OPP's version is superior in every way. Unfortunately, Paradox's official opinion seems to be EVERYTHING IS CANON (from the original game) so the nuking of both the Ravnos as well as the Black Hand is 100% correct. So if the Baali did join the True Hand, they were presumably nuked with the rest of Enoch. Such a shame.</div> </div> </div> </div>And now, I will say something very unpopoular: I think that V20's version of the True Hand is both the weakest V20 book and the less coherent version of the TBH in the history of metaplot. It's a hodge-podge of very different factions, which fall together for .... no particular reasons. 2nd Generation cultists, Baali, Antediluvian cultists, feminist Cultists worshipping a deity whose children were killed by Antediluvians, fundamentalist defender of &quot;Old Clans&quot; and Mutant Faerie Vampires ... what exactly does V20 True Hand stands for?<br /> <br /> Took separately, all the factions in the book make for very interesting Cults: put together, I really struggle to get the reasoning behind lumping them together.<br /> <br /> The Hecata, who are very much criticized for being a strange collection of people with too distant motives, are really a Happy Family compared to V20 True Black Hand !<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-28T19:12:50-08:00","id":1473514,"title":"","content":"I have to agree with you about the True Hand. While there were individual things in the V20 book that I liked, on the whole it struck me as a mostly incoherent hodgepodge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-29T06:45:50-08:00","id":1473522,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1473514#post1473514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to agree with you about the True Hand. While there were individual things in the V20 book that I liked, on the whole it struck me as a mostly incoherent hodgepodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, it might even work better to split the subfactions up and treat V20\u2019s TBH book more like a proto-\u201cCult of the Blood Gods\u201d","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1328-chris24601","name":"Chris24601","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"520"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-29T07:35:43-08:00","id":1473523,"title":"","content":"I did feel the factionalism was weird. Shouldn't the True Hand be like 100 or 200 guys tops?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-29T22:39:57-08:00","id":1473556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1473514#post1473514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to agree with you about the True Hand. While there were individual things in the V20 book that I liked, on the whole it struck me as a mostly incoherent hodgepodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have never read the V20 Black Hand book, and the comments here makes me feel like I should get a copy, and start a &quot;Where I read&quot; thread. Tell me if that's a bad idea...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby","name":"James_Willoughby","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar317_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T12:11:24-08:00","id":1473592,"title":"","content":"Go ahead please! We need more True Black Hand in our unlives!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12590-manfr","name":"Manfr","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"449"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T17:03:35-08:00","id":1473610,"title":"","content":"So what is everyone's favorite and least favorite cult from this book?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-01-30T20:08:39-08:00","id":1473627,"title":"","content":"What are the Withered Ones?<br /> <br /> What are the most interesting groups under &quot;Dreams of Golconda&quot;?<br /> <br /> What are the most interesting groups under &quot;Eschatological Thoughts&quot;?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1208-grumpy-rpg-reviews","name":"Grumpy RPG Reviews","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1208_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T14:20:57-08:00","id":1474516,"title":"","content":"I already bought and read the book, I enjoyed it. Forbidden Religions is an interesting supplement which introduces cool cults. I liked the Praesidium and the Spear of Orthia as playable cults, and the Withered and the Soldiers of the Adversary as antagonist. I also get the easter egg reference to the Baali character, Annazir.<br /> <br /> About the Talmahera, well, it is fine. Just fine, they have find a way to recover some of their significance, but taking distance from the errors of the past. They notably disregard the recruitment of new neonates and they do not use Oblivion, never. Maybe for the consequences the discipline had in the past.<br /> <br /> The worst thing, for me, about FR was again the lack of research with the Spanish culture. As already happened with Aluc Romas de Leon, we receive a new character with an inexistent surname, Maria del Torro. I am thankful for having the South of Europe depicted in the book, but this is not the way, do not emphasize the exoticism of foreign countries letting them being ruled by mad cults with inexistent names, please.<br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar317_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"317\" data-vbnamecard=\"317\">James_Willoughby</a> , I agree with the others in that The guide of the Talmahera is probably not the best book of V20, with a mix of incoherent ideas that rivals the Dirtys secrets of the black hand, and with a chronicle that is hard to play, hard to storytell and even hard to understand. They also included the rules from Dark ages mage there, the Maeghar, garou abominations, advanced diablerie, demon-hunters baali and many more bizarre ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24202,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","user":"Justycar","date":". 02-12-2022, 05:23 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24202-justycar","name":"Justycar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24202_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"320"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-02-12T14:35:47-08:00","id":1474518,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Justycar</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1464604-forbidden-religions-is-now-out-to-backers?p=1474516#post1474516\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I already bought and read the book, I enjoyed it. Forbidden Religions is an interesting supplement which introduces cool cults. I liked the Praesidium and the Spear of Orthia as playable cults, and the Withered and the Soldiers of the Adversary as antagonist. I also get the easter egg reference to the Baali character, Annazir.<br /> <br /> About the Talmahera, well, it is fine. Just fine, they have find a way to recover some of their significance, but taking distance from the errors of the past. They notably disregard the recruitment of new neonates and they do not use Oblivion, never. Maybe for the consequences the discipline had in the past.<br /> <br /> The worst thing, for me, about FR was again the lack of research with the Spanish culture. <b>As already happened with Aluc Romas de Leon, we receive a new character with an inexistent surname, Maria del Torro. I am thankful for having the South of Europe depicted in the book, but this is not the way, do not emphasize the exoticism of foreign countries letting them being ruled by mad cults with inexistent names, please.</b><br /> <br /> ---<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/317-james_willoughby\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar317_2.jpeg');\